<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:47:26Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Fact Check: False video alleges Berlin votes destroyed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a22b17a5936c44854f1e97b3bdb843590758d5c02885eb3b56366b92d0c71a75</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:46:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T18:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-false-video-alleges-berlin-votes-destroyed/a-79333344--411939a21d7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-false-video-alleges-berlin-votes-destroyed/a-79333344?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A video claiming to show AfD postal ballots being destroyed has gone viral ahead of Berlin's September 20 election. DW Fact Check examines the footage, the accounts sharing it and how widely it is really being viewed.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>German police probe arson attack on Wuppertal synagogue</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:37134173414646a351c117d28fd037f6de0e3c0c0b7a12e951893c35cdb2a4e9</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:46:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T15:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-police-probe-arson-attack-on-wuppertal-synagogue/a-79331270--dce70b32746f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-police-probe-arson-attack-on-wuppertal-synagogue/a-79331270?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The man detained shortly after allegedly trying to set fire to Wuppertal's synagogue made antisemitic comments to the arresting officers, prosecutors say. The 37-year-old Afghan citizen also had knives in his apartment.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz government approves fuel-price discount</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8780b93f6715b27c49d4324611f937d3ff2b629b24b3717cdd1b0f96a00c1606</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:47:26Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T11:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-government-approves-fuel-price-discount/live-79324526--2cf319e4f7c9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-government-approves-fuel-price-discount/live-79324526?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's coalition government is grappling with record-high fuel prices ahead of two state elections this weekend.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Third malaria death linked to Frankfurt Airport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe058018ca9af90ce44e70199cd8b04a2b904f84102601772b31d3b9836c04d0</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:46:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T16:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-third-malaria-death-linked-to-frankfurt-airport/a-79315012--d744a8a0ae06.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-third-malaria-death-linked-to-frankfurt-airport/a-79315012?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two new malaria cases have been registered this week near Frankfurt airport, two months after cases first emerged.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Mysterious explosions reported in Frankfurt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7721ca67b250c8f7022d793cf8f2806ca067191a6c9fb07b8a04709e1558b778</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:46:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T08:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-mysterious-explosions-reported-in-frankfurt/live-79300494--1397711c1e30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-mysterious-explosions-reported-in-frankfurt/live-79300494?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A cafe and kiosk were damaged overnight in Frankfurt, in what police said are the latest in a series of mysterious blasts in the area. Meanwhile, diesel prices in Germany have hit an all-time high. More on DW.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Airport malaria in Germany remains infrequent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a15b420a1a0d05d1293820eb3a0f6fd2d09a8ceb2565b8544e63a26247dab60</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:46:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T18:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/airport-malaria-in-germany-remains-infrequent/a-79333920--b6e9f1b4961f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/airport-malaria-in-germany-remains-infrequent/a-79333920?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An outbreak of malaria at Frankfurt Airport this summer has raised alarm. Experts believe parasites probably arrived in a passenger's luggage. But with the onset of fall, the risks of contracting the disease are low.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Dual citizenship means Germany now in competition for talent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc24a8e4254503b298496c84e76dfe48333b3dd03fa6426e384a2c58936ee876</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:46:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T14:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dual-citizenship-means-germany-now-in-competition-for-talent/a-79330797--d43696518a30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dual-citizenship-means-germany-now-in-competition-for-talent/a-79330797?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Coach Jürgen Klopp has named several players to his first Germany squad who are eligible to play for other countries. Some still aren't committed to playing for thje national team long-term.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Is it possible to replace the chancellor?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:90738258b231ea1e1db52db5cb7cf5d93fe6cd23f3e9f41074e07fb273aa2808</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:47:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T12:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-is-it-possible-to-replace-the-chancellor/a-79313623--5363f1668974.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-is-it-possible-to-replace-the-chancellor/a-79313623?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz's record-low approval ratings have emboldened his opponents. There are three ways to remove a chancellor from office in Germany.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>'No compromises': Far-right AfD has few potential partners</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92c4d7472a293258a6e079be9eff13091494972bb62011a9fba2e119ac572b6e</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:46:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T12:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/no-compromises-far-right-afd-has-few-potential-partners/a-79326208--c5bd1a26f736.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/no-compromises-far-right-afd-has-few-potential-partners/a-79326208?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's far-right AfD party is riding high after its latest electoral triumph in Saxony-Anhalt. But one question remains: Does it actually want to govern?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Oktoberfest 2026: Everything you need to know</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3cbccf9af32cdf63c9de6475900a5f472f85406f291fd41048d07be45ce9b4c0</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:46:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T08:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/oktoberfest-2026-everything-you-need-to-know/a-79311285--1e3ee9d16248.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/oktoberfest-2026-everything-you-need-to-know/a-79311285?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">This year, AI will be used to manage overcrowded situations. Find all the numbers surrounding the fest — including the price of water!</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Saint, sinner or feminist icon: How Mary Magdalene's image evolved through time</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:10475d99568ef46e6b05f329349b3794a26cad58625799bdf37d419860531e14</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:46:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T07:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saint-sinner-or-feminist-icon-how-mary-magdalene-s-image-evolved-through-time/a-79293868--1a6f3ade345e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saint-sinner-or-feminist-icon-how-mary-magdalene-s-image-evolved-through-time/a-79293868?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From "Apostle of the Apostles" to prostitute, Mary Magdalene has been assigned a wide variety of roles, as a new exhibition shows.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Elversberg: Bundesliga newcomers from tiny town make waves</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e1008e513888d9b989db3dbc70cc7058483d779cfedd92bb0f166d4c67592fe</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:46:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483--9d72d35ebb6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A team from a small southwestern German town of just 7,000 inhabitants made history by sealing promotion to become the 59th club to play in the Bundesliga. Elversberg has got off to a memorable start.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
